				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Back in GT, we need someone to talk to our server. For Carp, that is {{gtClass:CarpServerClient}}. It opens a socket, writes frames, reads frames, and turns the responses into objects. Most of its methods send exactly one command, like this one:"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "9AiMD6PaQbSiHOc3q7FuWQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "{{gtMethod:CarpServerClient>>#evalSource:session:|expanded}}"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "kCwDqYBKTJiq3qAFBOfUbg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The answer to an eval is a {{gtClass:CarpEvalResult}}: the source, the session, the exit code, the printed value, and whatever the program wrote to stdout and stderr. It has views for all of those, so even before anything else works, evaluating a cell gives us something to look at."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "u/SzKUucSbiwQaHvdWtCvA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Two things turned out to matter more than I expected. The first is starting the server. Nobody wants to start a server by hand before opening a notebook (I certainly don’t), so the client starts one when nothing listens on its port. It also replaces a running server that was built from an older binary, which saved me from a lot of head-scratching ({{gtMethod:CarpServerClient>>#ensureServerRunning}})."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "k/ud2jvlSuOn7GNGCGMTzQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The second is errors. A cell that doesn’t compile is not a protocol error, it is a perfectly normal answer that happens to contain the compiler’s complaints. So we keep the two apart: {{gtClass:CarpServerError}} is only for a server that can’t be reached or answers nonsense, and everything the compiler says comes back as data."
			}
		]
	},
